feat(fleet): add 14 ship-avatar personae for bot identity

Generates the visual identity for each of the 14 fleet ships - used as the
bot user avatar on GitHub PR comments (pd-code-reviewer[bot], etc.) and as
the chip art in the PD dashboard.

Each ship has three sizes:
  assets/ship-avatars/<name>/avatar-512.png   GitHub-bot avatar
  assets/ship-avatars/<name>/avatar-128.png   dashboard chip
  assets/ship-avatars/<name>/avatar-64.png    inline mention chip

Ships: code-reviewer, red-team, test-author, tautology-sniffer, tenderfoot,
augur, gardener, qa, test-hunter, documentarian, simplifier, cartographer,
spark, spider - grouped by family in ROSTER.md.

Style: flat editorial illustration with an architectural-blueprint sensibility,
strict four-color brand palette (cobalt #003fb8, sage #006b5f, cream #f2eee6,
ebony #1f1f1f). Each avatar is a character (face + role-prop), not a logo.
Distinct silhouette at 64px so the avatar tells you who is talking at a glance.

Generated via Nano Banana Pro (gemini-3-pro-image-preview). The runnable
script is preserved at scripts/ship-avatars/generate_fleet.py so any single
ship can be regenerated with `python3 scripts/ship-avatars/generate_fleet.py
--only <name> --force` without disturbing the others.

42 PNGs (14 ships * 3 sizes) + ROSTER.md + generator script.


